  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{k},\\, & 3\\le x\\le 5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in S$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nFor the given function, the second condition states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{x}{k}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the integral on the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{x}{k}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2k}]}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & =(\\frac{25}{2k}-\\frac{9}{2k}) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2k} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{k}=1\\,\u27f9\\,k=8.\n$$",
